  "notes": "{喚|わめ}く implies loud, uncontrolled shouting or screaming, often with a negative connotation suggesting the person is being unreasonable, hysterical, or obnoxious.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive)\n- No transitive pair\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{大声|おおごえ}→大声：09592_oogoe⟧で{喚|わめ}く: to scream at the top of one's lungs\n- ⟦{泣|な}き→泣く：00655_naku⟧{喚|わめ}く: to cry and scream (compound verb)\n- {喚|わめ}き{散|ち}らす: to scream wildly, make a scene\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{叫|さけ}ぶ→叫ぶ：02108_sakebu⟧: to shout, to scream (more neutral, can be positive)\n- ⟦{怒鳴|どな}る→怒鳴る：05340_donaru⟧: to yell angrily (specifically angry tone)\n- ⟦{騒|さわ}ぐ→騒ぐ：01195_sawagu⟧: to make noise, be rowdy (broader meaning)\n\nREGISTER:\n{喚|わめ}く carries a strongly negative nuance. Using it to describe someone implies disapproval of their behavior.",
